org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b9/Robert_E_Lee_Monument_at_Lee_Circle._New_Orleans_Louisiana_%28cropped%29.jpg/960px-Robert_E_Lee_Monument_at_Lee_Circle._New_Orleans_Louisiana_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"St. Patrick's Church (New Orleans)","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":29.946644,"lo":-90.069839,"d":1137,"ds":"St. Patrick's Church is a Catholic church and parish in the Archdiocese of New Orleans, Louisiana, United States. The parish was founded in 1833, and the current structure was completed in 1840.","wpu":"St. Patrick's Church (New Orleans)","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/eb/StPatricksChurchNO.JPG/960px-StPatricksChurchNO.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Contemporary Arts Center (New Orleans)","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":29.943732,"lo":-90.072818,"d":1167,"ds":"The Contemporary Arts Center, New Orleans is an arts complex located in historic downtown New Orleans. Founded in 1976, the center plays host to events and performances from visual arts to concert performances and lectures. General gallery admission is free to Louisiana residents, with varying hours and ticket arrangements for concerts and other special events.","wpu":"Contemporary Arts Center (New Orleans)","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b0/Contemporary_Arts_Center_New_Orleans.jpg/960px-Contemporary_Arts_Center_New_Orleans.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"400 Poydras Tower","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":29.9485,"lo":-90.0679,"d":1199,"ds":"400 Poydras Tower, formerly known as the Texaco Center, located at 400 Poydras Street in the Central Business District of New Orleans, Louisiana, is a 32-story, 442 feet (135 m)-tall skyscraper. Built in 1983, this modern office tower features more than 620,000 square feet (58,000 m2) of office space with an average of 22,000 rentable square feet per floor. The building is leased by Beau Box Commercial Real Estate.","wpu":"400 Poydras Tower","img":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/4/4b/400_Poydras_New_Orleans.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled"},{"n":"St. Alphonsus Church (New Orleans, Louisiana)","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":29.930556,"lo":-90.073611,"d":1460,"ds":"St. Alphonsus Church (French: Église Saint-Alphonse) is a historic former church building at 2029 Constance Street in New Orleans, Louisiana. Completed in 1857, it is one of the few surviving national examples of a richly multi-colored church interior predating the 1870s, and a high quality example of ecclesiastical Italianate architecture.","wpu":"St. Alphonsus Church (New Orleans, Louisiana)","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3c/StAlph26Oct07Palm.jpg/960px-StAlph26Oct07Palm.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Plaza Tower (New Orleans)","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":29.946389,"lo":-90.076667,"d":1634,"ds":"Plaza Tower is a 45-story, 531-foot (162 m) skyscraper in New Orleans, Louisiana, designed in the modern style by Leonard R. Spangenberg, Jr. & Associates. Located in the Central Business District (CBD), it is the third tallest building in both the city of New Orleans and the state of Louisiana.","wpu":"Plaza Tower (New Orleans)","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/25/CBD11Oct07PlazaTower.jpg/960px-CBD11Oct07PlazaTower.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Civic Theatre (New Orleans)","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":29.94953,"lo":-90.07421,"d":1659,"ds":"The Civic Theatre is a 1,200-seat theater located in New Orleans, Louisiana. The theatre was originally built in 1906 and is used for concerts, plays, films, corporate events and private parties.","wpu":"Civic Theatre (New Orleans)","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4d/JoeSeidersNP.jpg/960px-JoeSeidersNP.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"}],"about":{"ds":"New Orleans (commonly known as NOLA or The Big Easy, among other nicknames) is a consolidated city-parish located along the Mississippi River in the U.S. state of Louisiana. With a population of 383,997 at the 2020 census, New Orleans is the most populous city in Louisiana, the second-most populous in the Deep South (after Atlanta), and the twelfth-most populous in the Southeastern United States; the New Orleans metropolitan area, with about 1 million residents, is the 59th-most populous metropolitan area in the United States. New Orleans serves as a major port and commercial hub for the broader Gulf Coast region.","wpu":"New Orleans","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cb/New_Orleans_from_the_Air_September_2019_-_Central_Business_District_Skyline_%28cropped%29.jpg/960px-New_Orleans_from_the_Air_September_2019_-_Central_Business_District_Skyline_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},"wk":"2026-10-18"}